PATCH 470: MGAVIDEO driver-private-segment functions 400b/4030/405e rebuilt (windshield-object frontier,
slice 6) -- the sprite position / palette-bank / shade-table services the kind-6 renderer calls via
[0x668]/[0x674].

These functions start with `mov ds,[ss:0x70a]`: their variables (0x58a/0x58c screen pos, 0x58e shade,
0x5bd bank, 0x5bf/0x5cb bank tables) live in the driver's PRIVATE segment word[DGROUP:0x70a], not in
DGROUP -- the decompile's DAT_1000_c5xx macros (DGROUP-based) and the raw `*(int *)0x58e` host derefs
were both wrong (patch 466's 3fca is corrected to the same base).  405e fills the 256-byte shade table at
DGROUP:0x1448 (es=ss) and decrements the entries of the bank's bright-colour list; 4030 selects the bank
(ax>=0xc -> 10, CF=1) and resets the shade cache; 400b stores the sprite anchor.  asm-verified vs
re_out/fist_mga_image.bin 0x400b-0x40b5.
